00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:49.210
So let me set up a
time series graph.

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:51.910
I need a date range, I use
actually the time stamp

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:55.540
in which the data is coming in.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:58.150
And let's say I want to see
how much traffic comes in

00:13:58.150 --> 00:13:59.170
by continent.

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:03.070
So I select as a
breakdown, the continent.

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:06.670
Destination
continent, and I want

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:10.120
to see not how many
records, but how many bytes

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:12.820
have been sent between
these, from these continent,

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:16.210
or to these continents.

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:17.975
And because half
the traffic comes in

00:14:17.975 --> 00:14:20.920
and half the traffic goes out,
most of those are of no use,

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:24.230
I want to filter these, so
I'm going to add this filter.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:26.710
And it runs the BigQuery
queries in the background,

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:28.870
